Z||000004||maryjane||06-01-2001||12:33 AM||||Well, I dropped flares too, from a CH-53 many nights in Viet Nam. They were big ones, cylinder shaped about 16"x 36" we dropped down a tube in the floor of the cargo area. I've seen them from the ground too, a lot. You're right, even witha chute they drop rapidly and even though they may be carried by the wind somewhat, ten miles would be about as far as I would think they could go before burning out or hitting the ground. <BR>Don't think the boomerang lights are flares.<BR>along the same line any of you ever heard of or saw the Marfa Lights in Southwest Texas. I was a skeptic till I drove down ther and saw them my self. really strange. Do a web search if you are interested.<BR>Don||||reg||1
