Z||000011||AusFiero||06-05-2001||08:22 AM||||I can believe the are not of this world/time theories. I have seen 2 UFO. 1 with about 100 other people. It never made the news even though it was big as a mountain. That was in 1977.<P>Seen another about 2 years ago with my total non believer in such stuff wife. Well she didn't believe until then anyway.<P>The lakes stuff sound intriguing too. We have huge waterways and lakes under our Great Sandy Desert. Divers have gone in one and found waterways hundreds of kilometres long in a seemingly lifeless land.<P>On rogers comments I have also heard many theories the same as his. The future one always sticks in my head as possible. <P>If we could travel through time in the future look at evolution to see what you would be looking at. In the past we was very stocky and boney, then we progressed to what we are now. I see the future with more use of the brain and eyes than any other part being the age of what we are calling aliens. It is how we would evolve if we stay in front of screens and do less manual labour as a whole.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||1
